WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:18.000
EPA 608 is not optional. You cannot legally touch refrigerant without it.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:36.000
EPA 608 has four certification types. Type I covers small appliances —
factory-charged systems with 5 lbs or less. Type II covers high-pressure systems
including R-410A, R-22, and R-134a. Type III covers low-pressure systems like

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:54.000
Universal is the most valuable for a working technician. Each type requires a
separate exam section. To earn Universal you must pass all four sections — Core
plus Types I, II, and III.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:01:12.000
Certification does not expire but you must keep your card. Since 2018 you must
show your certification card to purchase any refrigerant.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:30.000
Get Universal. Type II alone limits your career. Universal opens every door —
residential, commercial, industrial.

